          "text": "10 MILLION HITS OF LSD.\n\nThat's how much Harvard chemist Leonard Pickard absorbed through his skin one night in 1998.\n\nHe was on a ladder in his Santa Fe lab, decanting a flask of pure LSD at 2 AM.\n\nHe slipped.\nThe flask shattered.\nHe was drenched head to toe.\n\nNow, if this were just normal LSD, he would have been fine. But the flask contained:\n\n𝗠𝗲𝘁𝗵𝘆𝗹𝗲𝗻𝗲 𝗰𝗵𝗹𝗼𝗿𝗶𝗱𝗲.\n\nWithin seconds, the solvent drove every drop of LSD through his skin & into his blood.\n\nHe stripped naked, blasted himself in the emergency shower, then stumbled into a field and collapsed.\n\nHe heard cosmic choirs of angels.\nSaw every version of himself dissolve.\nTime and identity fell apart into pure light.\n\nAnd through the peak of the largest LSD dose in human history, one message rang out:\n\n𝗔𝗹𝗹 𝘄𝗼𝘂𝗹𝗱 𝗯𝗲 𝗼𝗸𝗮𝘆.\n\nHe woke up the next morning. \nNo brain damage. No lingering effects.\nCleaned up the lab & went back to work.\n\n(probably had the best day of his life)"
